em up so all in now  they're like 40 50 60 000  in but then the houses were worth over  100 grand  they were and then they were selling  them and making  serious serious cash lots of class  cash for buying and selling you see in  the uk  if you buy a house for 40 grand and you  spend 20 grand on it and you put 16 all  together  if you do it right it might be worth 70  80 grand  but not like 120 not like in the states  so  that was really quite exciting to me i  wanted to do some flips out there  um the things that were harder was  i'm not 100 on the  agents as in it was more difficult just  to get appointments in england i find  that when you book a viewing your book a  viewing  it's in whereas in the states people  kept cancelling viewings not showing  because i hadn't confirmed enough  so i i personally find the uk the agents  easier to deal with but that might  because i'm just used to the agents  also the uk because it's a small island  everything's close by  so you don't have to drive around that  much and because it's a small island as  well  i think things you can be more confident  that things are going to rent  maybe so that's my that's my thoughts i  mean i wasn't i was only there a week  i'd love to go back but yeah uk versus  us  both are good just in different ways  okay next question paul anthony says  is 64 too old to get involved also see  you on the next birmingham crash course  uh  paul 64 is definitely not too old to get  involved  um we've had 72 year olds coming down to  the crash course and they've  loved it and gone and done deals um so  look forward to seeing you there  final question jack farquhar  oh geez i'm really struggling to  pronounce their names i am sorry but the  question's great  what do you look out for in a good  property management company both single  and  multi-layer if you're getting a property  manager  for a multi-let hmo it's really  important that they specialize in  multi-let's don't get a high street  agent  to manage 